    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The borough’s name honors Kennet, Wiltshire, England, and the “Square” refers to the original one‑square‑mile land grant from William Penn.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kennett_Square%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Kennett Square’s downtown, built between 1875 and 1924, is listed on the National Register of Historic Places and showcases Colonial Revival, Victorian, and Federal styles.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.brandywinevalley.com/towns-and-villages/kennett-square/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Longwood Gardens, a world‑famous botanical garden, lies just three miles from Kennett Square, making the area a green oasis.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kennett_Square%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1777, British General Sir William Howe marched troops through Kennett Square on their way to the Battle of Brandywine during the Revolutionary War.",
